{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-mat-14-1","title":"Matthew 14:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Herod's opinion of Christ. 3 Wherefore John Baptist was beheaded. 13 Jesus departs into a desert place, 15 where he feeds five thousand men with five loves and two fishes. 22 He walks on the sea to his disciples; 34 and landing at Gennesaret, heals the sick by the touch of the hem of his garment.</p>\n<p>Herod.This was Herod Antipas, the son of Herod the Great, by Malthace, and tetrarch of Galilee and Per�a, which produced a revenue of 200 talents a year. He married the daughter of Aretas, king of Arabia, whom he divorced in order to marry Herodias, the wife of his brother Philip, who was still living. Aretas, to revenge the affront which Herod had offered his daughter, declared war against him, and vanquished him after an obstinate engagement. This defeat, Josephus assures us, the Jews considered as a punishment for the death of John the Baptist. Having gone to Rome to solicit the title of king, he was accused by Agrippa of carrying on a correspondence with Artabanus king of Parthia, against the Romans, and was banished by the emperor Caius to Lyons, and thence to Spain, where he and Herodias died in exile.</p>\n<p>Mr 6:14-16; 8:15; Lu 9:7-9; 13:31,32; 23:8-12,15; Ac 4:27 Tetrarch. Lu 3:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-2","title":"Matthew 14:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>This. 11:11; 16:14; Mr 8:28; Joh 10:41 do shew forth themselves in him. or, are wrought by him.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-3","title":"Matthew 14:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Herod. 4:12; Mr 6:17; Lu 3:19,20; Joh 3:23,24 Herodias'.This infamous woman was the daughter of Aristobulus and Bernice, and granddaughter of Herod the Great.</p>\n<p>his. Lu 13:1 Philip's.Herod Philip, son of Herod the Great and Mariamne.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-4","title":"Matthew 14:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Le 18:16; 20:21; De 25:5,6; 2Sa 12:7; 1Ki 21:19; 2Ch 26:18,19 Pr 28:1; Isa 8:20; Mr 6:18; Ac 24:24,25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-5","title":"Matthew 14:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>when. Mr 6:19,20; 14:1,2; Ac 4:21; 5:26 because. 21:26,32; Mr 11:30-32; Lu 20:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-6","title":"Matthew 14:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>birth-day. Ge 40:20; Es 1:2-9; 2:18; Da 5:1-4; Ho 1:5,6; Mr 6:21-23 the daughter. 22:24 danced. Es 1:10-12 before them. Gr. in the midst.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-7","title":"Matthew 14:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Es 5:3,6; 7:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-8","title":"Matthew 14:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>being. 2Ch 22:2,3; Mr 6:24 Give. 1Ki 18:4,13; 19:2; 2Ki 11:1; Pr 1:16; 29:10 a charger. Nu 7:13,19,84,85; Ezr 1:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-9","title":"Matthew 14:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>the king. 1; Mr 6:14 sorry. 5; 27:17-26; Da 6:14-16; Mr 6:20,26; Lu 13:32; Joh 19:12-16 Ac 24:23-27; 25:3-9 the oath's. Nu 30:5-8; Jud 11:30,31,39; 21:1,7-23; 1Sa 14:24,28,39-45; 25:22 1Sa 25:32-34; 28:10; 2Ki 6:31-33; Ec 5:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-10","title":"Matthew 14:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>and beheaded. 17:12; 21:35,36; 22:3-6; 23:34-36; 2Ch 36:16; Jer 2:30; Mr 6:27-29 Mr 9:13; Lu 9:9; Re 11:7 the prison.Josephus informs us that John the Baptist was imprisoned and beheaded by Herod in the strong castle of Machaerus, which he describes as situated about 60 stadia east of Jordan, not far from where the river discharges itself into the Dead Sea.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-11","title":"Matthew 14:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>and given. Ge 49:7; Pr 27:4; 29:10; Jer 22:17; Eze 16:3,4; 19:2,3; 35:6; Re 16:6 Re 17:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-12","title":"Matthew 14:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>took. 27:58-61; Ac 8:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-13","title":"Matthew 14:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>1,2; 10:23; 12:15; Mr 6:30-33; Lu 9:10-17; Joh 6:1-15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-14","title":"Matthew 14:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>and was. 9:36; 15:32-39; Mr 6:34; 8:1,2; 9:22; Lu 7:13; 19:41; Joh 11:33-35 Heb 2:17; 4:15; 5:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-15","title":"Matthew 14:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>his. Mr 6:35,36; Lu 9:12 send. 15:23; Mr 8:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-14-16","title":"Matthew 14:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>they. 2Ki 4:42-44; Job 31:16,17; Pr 11:24; Ec 11:2; Lu 3:11; Joh 13:29 2Co 8:2,3; 9:7,8</p>"},{"id":"t